Buoyancy and wind can compete with mechanical pressure (@cm-stack-wind: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/CONTAM-Multizone-Airflow-and-Contaminants-NIST.lingua#r_5HECDC480RSYAJ3SQ2QNFHCN46", #source "../sources/Air-Cleaning-Handbook-DOE.lingua#r_09QPEZ76E9W6HS7R55X2K8TB3X", #clean-manufacturing "An-open-door-can-carry-flow-in-both-directions.lingua#r_7AZQQX7PSG2H8KGFB79TTN3F7Z") { r_44PV55ESMT6BHNTS2DT5XSA4JS
**Read:** [Multizone airflow and contaminants — Dols and Polidoro, CONTAM 3.4](../sources/CONTAM-Multizone-Airflow-and-Contaminants-NIST.lingua#r_5HECDC480RSYAJ3SQ2QNFHCN46), wind and hydrostatic airflow models; [Air-cleaning systems — DOE-HDBK-1169-2022](../sources/Air-Cleaning-Handbook-DOE.lingua#r_09QPEZ76E9W6HS7R55X2K8TB3X), section 4.5.5; the full readings in [Hydrostatic balance, gravity and density variation](../../../physics/fluid-dynamics/statics/Hydrostatic-balance-gravity-and-density-variation.lingua#r_0BMK5JN8XP72JR1WQG5B52PFMS) and [Boussinesq flow, natural convection, plumes and instability](../../../physics/fluid-dynamics/geophysical/Boussinesq-flow-natural-convection-plumes-and-instability.lingua#r_3D346A9GVA8D8T39K4KHG0X3W0).

With uniform density in each adjacent zone and height z upward, Δp(z)=Δp(0)−g(ρ1−ρ2)z. A pressure measured at one height can therefore differ in sign from another height. Thermal plumes and stratification can additionally alter local transport.

A simplified external wind term is Δpw=½ρU²ΔCp. For hypothetical ρ=1.2 kg/m³, U=5 m/s and ΔCp=0.6, it is 9 Pa. The pressure coefficient depends on direction, building geometry and surroundings; the example does not supply a site coefficient.

**Work:** Compare the wind scale with the two-room example. Find the neutral height of a stated hydrostatic pressure difference. Draw nearby intakes, exhausts and possible re-entry paths. Explain what additional evidence is needed before converting a prevailing-wind diagram into a reliable intake or discharge location.

